# DTF tier manifest: bazel-bzlmod-registry  (artifact-keeper#2858, #4429; both
# shipped in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a run-time-filled upstream (upstreams.mock-files,
# from the proxy-download-ledger tier) playing the Bazel Central Registry:
# bazel_registry.json and modules/<name>/{metadata.json,<version>/...} under
# /bcr, with per-path request counters. Proxy-cache sidecars are aged through
# a throwaway postgres:16-alpine container with --volumes-from the backend.
#
# THE BEHAVIOUR
# #2858  /bazel/{repo} serves the Bzlmod registry layout. Hosted: PUT
#        modules/{name}/{version}/{file}; metadata.json is generated from the
#        versions that have a MODULE.bazel (component-wise sorted, empty
#        yanked_versions); a published file is never overwritten (409);
#        metadata.json cannot be PUT (400); source.json must be JSON (400);
#        bazel_registry.json is {"mirrors":[]}. Remote: proxies the upstream
#        registry; files under modules/{name}/{version}/ are immutable,
#        bazel_registry.json and metadata.json take the 300 s mutable TTL.
#        Virtual: merges metadata.json across members, resolves files by
#        member priority.
# #4429  (documented in docs/bazel.md) a module name a hosted member publishes
#        shadows that name on every remote member: only the hosted versions
#        are listed, a remote-only version of it is 404, and the remote is
#        never asked for it.
#
# THE PRIMITIVE FOR "15 MINUTES LATER": cached_at and expires_at in the
# entry's __cache_meta__.json are both moved back 900 s, as in the
# github-release-mirror tier.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on 1.10.0 (no /bazel route: every request 404), GREEN on
#              1.11.0 and main:
#              #2858 hosted PUTs 201; metadata.json ["1.0","1.2","1.10"] with
#                    {} yanked; MODULE.bazel / source.json byte-exact;
#                    bazel_registry.json {"mirrors":[]}.
#              #2858 overwrite 409 (bytes unchanged); PUT metadata.json 400;
#                    non-JSON source.json 400.
#              #2858 remote MODULE.bazel / metadata.json / bazel_registry.json
#                    are the upstream's; aged 15 minutes, the versioned file
#                    is served with no upstream request and metadata.json
#                    revalidates.
#              #2858/#4429 virtual (hosted p1, remote p2): rmod lists the
#                    remote's ["1.0","2.0"], hmod the hosted versions; with a
#                    hosted `common` 1.0 the virtual lists only ["1.0"],
#                    answers 404 for the remote's common/9.0, serves the hosted
#                    common/1.0 and the remote rmod/1.0, and the remote is never
#                    asked for common's metadata.json or files.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: a generic Remote over the same mock
#              BCR serves MODULE.bazel and metadata.json byte-exact and the
#              warm read does not go upstream.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 authenticated calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
